      "id": "a-fissures-courtes",
      "label": "A · Fissures courtes",
      "description": "Fêlures fines, directions différentes",
      "prompt": "Variation A: two distinct short natural stone fissures, well separated on two interior slabs. One begins at an inner mortar edge and bends twice inward to a tapered fine tip. The second starts at another internal corner and curves in a different orientation, with just one very small branch. Neither is a repeated diagonal slash or a symmetric Y. Deep muted charcoal recess, minuscule blue-grey edge light, NO violet and no glow. Hairline irregularity, no large ravine. Most slabs intact.",
