    {
      "id": "b-fracture-ramifiee",
      "label": "B · Fracture ramifiée",
      "description": "Un tracé irrégulier, localisé",
      "prompt": "Variation B: a single fine irregular stepped fracture, with two unequal small branching tips, on the two adjacent interior stones toward the front-right of the patch. Change direction with angular organic bends; follow a short part of an existing mortar seam then continue onto the next stone. Do not draw a long straight diagonal across the whole patch. Asymmetrical and delicate, tapered tips, subtle cool bevel. No radial impact star, circular hole, gouge, violet or glow. The crack is damage in solid stone, all stone pieces stay level.",
      "generatedPath": "C:/Users/A/.codex/generated_images/01a15ce9-67f0-77e2-a485-14b09d65f5da/exec-fff6e7b9-624d-468d-b978-bf98c5756e38.png",
