    {
      "id": "c-veine-corrompue",
      "label": "C · Veine corrompue",
      "description": "Violet contenu dans une fissure",
      "prompt": "Variation C: one restrained violet corruption vein recessed into a narrow irregular fissure on one central-left slab, linking briefly to its internal mortar joint. A dark thin crack contains several separated purple glow segments, not a continuous neon line. Two very short unequal forks follow the stone plane. Small tight violet halo limited to the fissure lips, no wide light spill. Enough violet to remain visible at small size but subordinate to a hero or dungeon heart. No crystals, roots, holes or raised objects. It should feel embedded inside the stone.",
      "generatedPath": "C:/Users/A/.codex/generated_images/01a15ce9-67f0-77e2-a485-14b09d65f5da/exec-a4159246-9d72-4a0d-b399-d74085bc6465.png",
