    {
      "id": "d-racines-corrompues",
      "label": "D · Racines corrompues",
      "description": "Racines sombres dans les joints",
      "prompt": "Variation D: a small asymmetric cluster of thin dark-purple corrupted roots creeping tightly along two INNER mortar joints near the central-right stones. One or two thin tendrils cross only a short portion of a slab before tapering. Subtle violet veins and one tiny embedded violet shard at a joint junction, all very low and hugging the floor; no tall crystal, no crystal pile, no nest, no tentacle mass. Closely related to the corrupt wall material in reference 3, but less busy, smaller and flatter. Restrained compact violet focal point, with 80-90 percent of paving smooth and untouched.",
      "generatedPath": "C:/Users/A/.codex/generated_images/01a15ce9-67f0-77e2-a485-14b09d65f5da/exec-c5d44e70-5aac-4f2d-a990-59d7a4acbb7a.png",
